---
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | 559 Solutions"
  description="Draft terms for using the 559 Solutions website and its practical resources."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Terms of Use" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Site information</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lede">Draft terms for this website and its resources.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="narrow legal-content">
      <p class="legal-banner">OWNER AND LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED</p>
      <p><strong>Draft last updated:</strong> July 23, 2026</p>
      <p>
        These draft terms are a starting point for owner and legal review. They do not create guarantees about products, services, outcomes, or availability.
      </p>

      <h2>Informational purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Website content is provided for general educational and informational purposes. It is not legal, financial, security, or other regulated professional advice.
      </p>

      <h2>Products and services</h2>
      <p>
        A product or service is available only when the site displays a real destination and the owner confirms the applicable scope, price, license, support, delivery, and refund terms. Coming-soon pages are descriptions of planned work, not offers for sale.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Visitors should not attempt to disrupt the site, bypass security measures, submit unlawful material, or misuse forms and downloads.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property and licenses</h2>
      <p>
        Site text, visual identity, and original resources remain subject to applicable ownership and license terms. Each downloadable product should include its own license summary before publication.
      </p>

      <h2>External services and links</h2>
      <p>
        External checkout, scheduling, analytics, form, and embedded-content providers operate under their own terms. A link does not create a guarantee or endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        The owner may update site content, product status, and these draft terms. A reviewed effective date must be added before launch.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
